# 3. HDFS Metadata

Metadata means information about files and directories.

NameNode maintains important metadata using two main files.

## 3.1 FsImage

FsImage is a snapshot of the HDFS filesystem namespace at a particular checkpoint.

It contains information such as:

- Files
- Directories
- Permissions
- Ownership
- File-to-block mapping

## 3.2 EditLog

EditLog records changes made to the HDFS namespace.

Examples:

- Create file
- Delete file
- Rename file
- Create directory
- Change permissions

### Difference between FsImage and EditLog

| FsImage | EditLog |
|---|---|
| Stores namespace snapshot | Stores namespace changes |
| Represents a checkpoint | Records transactions after checkpoint |
| Used during NameNode recovery | Replays namespace changes |

