# 8. HDFS Fault Tolerance

Fault tolerance means the system can continue operating when some components fail.

HDFS provides fault tolerance through:

1. Block replication.
2. DataNode heartbeats.
3. Block reports.
4. Automatic re-replication.
5. Checksums for data integrity.

## Heartbeat

DataNodes periodically send heartbeat messages to NameNode.

This tells NameNode that the DataNode is alive.

If a DataNode stops sending heartbeats for the configured timeout period, NameNode marks it as dead.

## Block Report

DataNodes send block reports to NameNode.

A block report contains information about blocks stored by that DataNode.

## Automatic Re-replication

If a DataNode fails and blocks become under-replicated, NameNode can arrange additional replicas on available DataNodes.

