# 10. HDFS Installation and Configuration

Important configuration files:

```text
$HADOOP_HOME/etc/hadoop/
```

Main files:

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| core-site.xml | Default filesystem configuration |
| hdfs-site.xml | HDFS configuration |
| hadoop-env.sh | Hadoop environment settings |
| workers | Worker hostnames for daemon scripts |

## core-site.xml

Example:

```xml
<configuration>
    <property>
        <name>fs.defaultFS</name>
        <value>hdfs://localhost:9000</value>
    </property>
</configuration>
```

This specifies the default HDFS NameNode address.

## hdfs-site.xml

Example:

```xml
<configuration>
    <property>
        <name>dfs.replication</name>
        <value>1</value>
    </property>

    <property>
        <name>dfs.namenode.name.dir</name>
        <value>file:///home/aboxuser/hadoopdata/namenode</value>
    </property>

    <property>
        <name>dfs.datanode.data.dir</name>
        <value>file:///home/aboxuser/hadoopdata/datanode</value>
    </property>
</configuration>
```

### Important properties

| Property | Purpose |
|---|---|
| fs.defaultFS | Default filesystem URI |
| dfs.replication | Default replication factor |
| dfs.blocksize | Default block size |
| dfs.namenode.name.dir | NameNode metadata storage |
| dfs.datanode.data.dir | DataNode block storage |
| dfs.namenode.http-address | NameNode Web UI address |

