# 19. Advanced HDFS Commands

## 19.1 Replication

Set replication:

```bash
hdfs dfs -setrep 3 /data/file.txt
```

Set replication recursively:

```bash
hdfs dfs -setrep -R 2 /data
```

## 19.2 Extended Attributes

Read attributes:

```bash
hdfs dfs -getfattr -d /data/file.txt
```

Set an attribute:

```bash
hdfs dfs -setfattr -n user.comment -v test /data/file.txt
```

## 19.3 Snapshots

Enable snapshots:

```bash
hdfs dfsadmin -allowSnapshot /company
```

Create snapshot:

```bash
hdfs dfs -createSnapshot /company snap1
```

List snapshottable directories:

```bash
hdfs lsSnapshottableDir
```

List snapshots:

```bash
hdfs lsSnapshot /company
```

Access snapshot files:

```bash
hdfs dfs -ls /company/.snapshot/snap1/
```

Delete snapshot:

```bash
hdfs dfs -deleteSnapshot /company snap1
```

Compare snapshots:

```bash
hdfs snapshotDiff /company snap1 snap2
```

Compare snapshot with current live directory:

```bash
hdfs snapshotDiff /company snap1 .
```

## 19.4 Cache Administration

List cache directives:

```bash
hdfs cacheadmin -listDirectives
```

Show cache help:

```bash
hdfs cacheadmin -help
```

Create cache pool:

```bash
hdfs cacheadmin -addPool employee_pool
```

Add cache directive:

```bash
hdfs cacheadmin -addDirective \
-path /company/employees \
-pool employee_pool \
-replication 1
```

Remove cache directives for a path:

```bash
hdfs cacheadmin -removeDirectives -path /company/employees
```

**Note:** Caching requires DataNode memory caching configuration and suitable cache capacity.

